<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Guatemala</h1><p class="st-meta">1823 CE – 1847 CE · capital Guatemala City</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The largest member of the Central American Federation, scene of liberal reform under Mariano Gálvez and of Rafael Carrera's conservative rise.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-guatemala">Guatemala</a>, centre of the old Captaincy General, became one of the five states of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/federal-republic-of-central-america">Federal Republic of Central America</a> under the constitution of 1824, with its own head of state and assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala-city">Guatemala City</a>, which was also the federal capital until 1834.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state was the main battleground between liberals and conservatives. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mariano-galvez">Mariano Gálvez</a>, head of state from 1831, introduced civil marriage, the Livingston penal codes, land grants to foreign colonists and a head tax. When cholera struck in 1837, rural Maya and ladino communities rose under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-carrera">Rafael Carrera</a>, who took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala-city">Guatemala City</a> in 1838. The western highlands broke away as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-los-altos">State of Los Altos</a> until Carrera crushed it in 1840.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the federation dissolved, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-guatemala">Guatemala</a> acted as a sovereign state under conservative governments dominated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-carrera">Carrera</a>, in alliance with the church. On 21 March 1847 Carrera formally declared it the independent Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1823 CE – 1847 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type"